guide-entry-corporations = Corporations
guidebook-corporations-overview = This section lists the corporations that offer players their own proprietary technologies. Each corporation description is the same text shown when selecting it in the lobby.
guidebook-corporations-disk-overview = The first time a member of one of these corporations spawns during a round, they receive a sealed case containing a unique technology disk.
guidebook-corporations-territory-ring = A station under corporate control has an additional outline outside its faction territory on the mass scanner and BSS map. The outline uses the servicing corporation's color and displays its name along the circumference. Zoom in to read the name. Removing the corporate flag removes the outline; the territory's actual radius stays the same.
guidebook-corporation-tech-disk-heading = Corporate technology disk
guidebook-corporation-tech-disk-acquisition = The first time a member of this corporation spawns during a round, they receive a sealed case containing the disk shown below.
guidebook-corporation-tech-disk-usage = The case can only be opened with an ID card assigned to the matching corporation. Hold the disk and use it on a research server: its recipes will be added to that server's technology database and the disk will be consumed.
guidebook-hive-recognition = Chimeras recognize Hive members by a purple marker beside them. The marker follows actual Hive membership: removing a PDA does not hide it, and carrying someone else's ID card does not grant it.
guidebook-medical-biofabrication = Producing organs requires a medical biofabricator. Research Industrial Medicine, then Medical Biofabrication for 15,000 points at the research console. Connect a circuit imprinter to the same research server and print the board using 10 steel, 20 glass, 10 gold and 10 silver. Assemble the machine in a machine frame with the board, two matter bins and two manipulators. Connect the biofabricator to power and the research server, then load the materials for the desired organ. Corporate organs also require their corresponding technology disk.
